     {"question": "How does the sliding window algorithm work?", "answer": "The service tracks the count of requests and the timestamp of the last request. When a new request arrives, it checks if the time since last request exceeds the window. If so, the count resets to 1. Otherwise, it increments the count and checks against the limit."},
     {"question": "Can I use different limits for different endpoints?", "answer": "Yes, use different keys and options per endpoint. For example, rateLimitService.limit('api:upload:' + userId, { max: 10, windowSeconds: 60 }) for uploads and a different configuration for other endpoints."},
